    md: "A good discriminator, not answered well. Most knew to differentiate, but some could not handle a term with a negative power even though they had managed one earlier in the same paper, and some read the gradient off a coefficient as though the curve were $y = mx + c$. Credit was given for knowing the normal's gradient is the negative reciprocal, even where the tangent gradient was wrong. The examiners asked for more practice on normals specifically.",
    source: "ccea-cer:further-maths:2019-summer:FM1:Q11",
  },
  {
    type: "callout",
